Why vendored
------------
The application must remain a single self-contained artefact with no run-time
dependency on an external content network (spec 002-map-view, FR-018). A CDN
<script> tag is therefore not an option. These files are embedded into the
binary by the //go:embed assets/static/* directive in internal/web/server.go,
which recurses into this directory.

Only map *imagery* (tiles) is fetched at run time, and it is fetched by the
user's browser directly from the tile provider — never by the server
(FR-021).

Note on marker icons
--------------------
Leaflet's default marker uses marker-icon.png / marker-shadow.png / layers.png,
referenced by URL relative to leaflet.css. Those images are deliberately NOT
vendored: the map uses L.divIcon with text labels instead (research.md R9), so
no image assets are needed and there is no CSS-relative URL to rewrite.

Upgrading
---------
1. Download the three files from the new tag.
2. Update the version, date and SHA-256 values above.
3. Re-run: go test ./internal/web/... (asset-serving tests must stay green).
4. Re-run the quickstart browser checklist — Leaflet upgrades can change
   control markup and full-screen sizing behaviour.

Leaflet 2.x is intentionally NOT used: as of this writing it is pre-release
(2.0.0-alpha.1) and ESM-only, which would require a JavaScript module loader
in a project that deliberately has no JS build toolchain (research.md R1).
